WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.310
(audience cheering)

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:02.143
- Welcome back everybody,

00:00:02.143 --> 00:00:04.260
we are still here with Lisa
Whelchel and Rachel Bloom.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.220
Give it up.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.450
(audience cheering)

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:09.771
And we're having an
'80s celebration y'all.

00:00:09.771 --> 00:00:12.440
Well, I'm about celebrating
my upcoming 40th birthday.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.273
I'm very excited.

00:00:13.273 --> 00:00:14.941
I also wanted to use this week-long party

00:00:14.941 --> 00:00:17.480
to shine a light on courses
that are close to my heart.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.131
Anyone who knows me at all,

00:00:19.131 --> 00:00:21.490
knows that I'm a huge animal lover.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:24.530
I always say that animals can
often be better than humans

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:26.290
'cause it's a true statement.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.123
Do you agree?

00:00:27.123 --> 00:00:29.010
(Kelly laughing)
- Yeah.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.296
- My dogs are amazing.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.780
There's a sanctuary just outside LA

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.760
that not only rescues animals in need,

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.020
they also invite humans
to come by and bond,

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.560
and they heal with the animals.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.700
It's really, really cool.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.470
From Kindred Spirits Care Farm,

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:45.050
let's say hi to Maria, Pierre the goat,

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:46.698
and Amaya the chicken.

00:00:46.698 --> 00:00:51.477
(audience cheering)
(bright upbeat music)

00:00:51.477 --> 00:00:53.894
Oh, my gosh.
- Oh my goodness.

00:00:55.478 --> 00:00:56.561
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:58.670
- [Maria] With a little diaper.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:00:59.770
- Wait, what is she?

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:00.964
Does she have a diaper on?

00:01:00.964 --> 00:01:02.194
- She's wearing a diaper.

00:01:02.194 --> 00:01:03.335
- Hello.
- Hi, hello.

00:01:03.335 --> 00:01:05.210
- Hello.
- Hi.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.360
- Oh, my gosh.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:07.330
Are we allowed to pet?

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.163
We're allowed to like...
- Of course.

00:01:08.163 --> 00:01:09.160
You wanna give him a carrot?
- Fine

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.040
- Can I put this here,

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.330
is that okay?
- Fine.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:12.490
Can I give a carrot?

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:13.330
- Can I grab her?

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:14.178
Would you hold this for a second?

00:01:14.178 --> 00:01:15.011
- Yes, got it.

00:01:15.011 --> 00:01:15.973
(Maria laughing)
Here you go.

00:01:15.973 --> 00:01:17.070
- Oh, okay, you're gonna babysit her.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:18.569
- Are we gonna be friends?

00:01:18.569 --> 00:01:20.191
Are we gonna be friends?

00:01:20.191 --> 00:01:21.440
- [Maria] He's like, oh,
if you give me a carrot,

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.276
we'll be best friends.

00:01:22.276 --> 00:01:23.110
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:23.943
How healing?

00:01:23.943 --> 00:01:24.776
I just gave him one.

00:01:24.776 --> 00:01:26.440
I didn't know how many you wanted to give.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:27.273
Well, hello and welcome

00:01:27.273 --> 00:01:28.106
to the show.
- Thank you.

00:01:28.106 --> 00:01:29.525
- Meet Rachel, meet Lisa.
- Hi.

00:01:29.525 --> 00:01:30.358
- Hi.
- Nice to meet you.

00:01:30.358 --> 00:01:31.327
Shall I gather my chicken
or you're okay with it?

00:01:31.327 --> 00:01:34.570
- I feel are our names,
Rachel, Lisa, Kelly,

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.340
these are like all names
from '80s movies as well,

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:37.580
and Maria it's like amazing.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:38.960
I just thought of that.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:40.640
Well, tell us about your animals here.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:41.580
So this is Pierre, right?

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:42.775
- This is Hanson Pierre,

00:01:42.775 --> 00:01:45.380
and was rescued about two years ago

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.050
with his girlfriend Perla.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:48.930
And then we have Amaya,

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:52.710
and she was recently rescued
off of a slaughter house truck,

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:54.710
and she came to us very sick.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.330
- [Kelly] Oh.
- And she had pneumonia,

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:58.946
and our director Karen
nursed her back to health.

00:01:58.946 --> 00:02:00.740
We weren't sure if she was gonna make it,

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.150
but now she loves sitting on lap.

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:03.676
She's like a lap chicken,

00:02:03.676 --> 00:02:05.980
and they're living their best lives

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:06.813
at the care farm.

00:02:06.813 --> 00:02:07.646
Come here, Pierre.
(audience applauding)

00:02:07.646 --> 00:02:09.180
- Pierre, you're so cute.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:10.070
You're so cute.

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:11.230
I'm not trying to stop you.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.730
- Doesn't he have amazing eyes?

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:14.090
- [Kelly] You want a carrot?

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:15.580
Oh my God, I just love how you eat it.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.444
So tell us more about the farm.

00:02:17.444 --> 00:02:22.290
- Well, our director, Karen,
started this care farm in 2013,

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.040
and she wanted a special place

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.751
that didn't just rescue animals,

00:02:25.751 --> 00:02:28.840
but helped rescue people who had trauma

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:30.784
or needed healing in some way.

00:02:30.784 --> 00:02:33.830
And so we have this beautiful space

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:37.070
with alpacas, emus...
(chicken clucks)

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:37.903
Oh, you wanna come down?

00:02:37.903 --> 00:02:38.736
Okay, okay.

00:02:38.736 --> 00:02:39.569
- She's like, this is my moment,

00:02:39.569 --> 00:02:41.312
let me shine, ma'am, let me shine.

00:02:41.312 --> 00:02:42.145
- Sorry.

00:02:42.145 --> 00:02:44.060
Have your moment, Amaya.
- Yeah.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:49.060
- Horses, a donkey, sheep,
goats, pigs, tortoises,

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.490
we have a great Pyrenees
named Hava, a dog.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:54.228
Yes, this is all our sweet babies.

00:02:54.228 --> 00:02:55.061
Pedro in the middle,

00:02:55.061 --> 00:02:55.894
the top middle.
- [Kelly] Oh my Gosh,

00:02:55.894 --> 00:02:57.500
are you just so happy all the time?

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.170
- [Maria] I know, it's pretty amazing

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.800
to go there and volunteer.
- [Kelly] It's so beautiful.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:03.190
- [Maria] And we also
have a community garden,

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:05.880
so if you're not into animals
and you still wanna be outside

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.237
and let nature heal you.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:07.237 --> 00:03:09.230
- [Maria] The Emus, they're hilarious.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.063
And yeah.

00:03:10.063 --> 00:03:11.500
- [Kelly] Oh my God, that's beautiful.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.610
- [Maria] And so we're working

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:15.100
on growing the garden and...
- Oh I got you boo, okay.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:16.320
- If he's too much I can take him.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:17.630
- Oh no, no, no.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:18.463
You haven't met Henry, my dog.

00:03:18.463 --> 00:03:19.626
(both laugh)

00:03:19.626 --> 00:03:21.210
He's in my lap usually and he's huge.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:22.043
- Aw.

00:03:22.043 --> 00:03:22.876
- He thinks he's small.
- Aw.

00:03:22.876 --> 00:03:23.900
- Oh, hi.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.210
Hey, I'm hungry too, I get it.
(guests mumbling)

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.370
I'm like waiting for lunch.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.250
- Amaya's over here.
- [Maria] Oh, okay.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.500
- [Kelly] So she's just hanging out.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:30.850
So visitors get to the farm,

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:33.450
and from the farm, they get
a unique experience, right?

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:34.283
So, what is that?
- Yeah.

00:03:34.283 --> 00:03:38.110
There's like tons of
experiences one can have.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.640
You can come and volunteer,

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:41.860
you can come and visit
just the regular public.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:43.804
We're open on Sundays from 10 to 2,

00:03:43.804 --> 00:03:47.944
but we also offer during
the week high school kids,

00:03:47.944 --> 00:03:50.240
or elementary school kids to come

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:51.620
and learn about the animals,

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:54.345
learn about horticulture,
learn about composting.

00:03:54.345 --> 00:03:56.235
- [Kelly] That's so cool.

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:57.690
I would love to have learned
that when I was a kid.

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:58.800
I mean, I would now I'm like 39,

00:03:58.800 --> 00:03:59.840
but like, yeah.
- [Maria] I know, me too.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:00.673
It's amazing,

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.250
and we also then have programs

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:05.510
for adults to come that
need healing, like veterans,

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:08.560
people living in sober
living homes, they can come,

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.549
and usually adults wanna
get their hands dirty,

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:12.780
so maybe they wanna scoop poop,

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:14.040
We got tons of that.
- Yeah.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:17.740
- They want to help build
a pen for the animals,

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:20.450
or fix it up or work in the gardens.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:21.283
- Have a purpose that's selfless,

00:04:21.283 --> 00:04:22.530
that's nice, yeah.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:24.390
- Exactly, and just being outside...

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.800
- One more.
- Oh.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.250
- Cherish the moment.
- Oh I'm so sorry.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:29.970
- Cherish the moment.
(Maria laughing)

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:30.810
Oh, I don't care.

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:33.480
like literally, I love
animals more than humans.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:36.480
So how do you see the farm
growing in the future?

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.360
- We have seven acres
and we'd love to expand.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.970
We have beautiful rocks and
boulders on the property,

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:44.090
so we'd love to be able
to fence them and so...

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:44.930
- Love him.
- yeah,

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:46.910
so the goats can run and jump

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:49.590
because goats and rocks
is like bliss, right?

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:50.423
- Yeah.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:52.280
- We wanna grow out our community garden,

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:54.470
and Karen, our director, her ultimate goal

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:56.143
is to have a walipini,

00:04:56.143 --> 00:04:59.830
which is a semi subterranean greenhouse

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:01.680
and use it as a workshop place

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:04.430
and to teach about
horticulture and gardening,

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:05.263
and, so yeah.

00:05:05.263 --> 00:05:06.096
- This is the coolest spot ever.

00:05:06.096 --> 00:05:07.353
- [Maria] You have to come, yeah.

00:05:07.353 --> 00:05:08.460
- Yes
- You should all come.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:09.570
It's really close too,

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:11.410
about 25 minutes from here.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.100
- And it's amazing that you can go

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.310
to such a peaceful place

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:16.391
that's within the bounds of Los Angeles

00:05:16.391 --> 00:05:19.980
and just relax and heal and
be amongst these cuties.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:21.420
- In such a busy city, yeah.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:22.430
'cause this is like, for me,

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:23.850
I grew up like out in the country,

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.810
so it's like, it's very different for me.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:27.710
Like I feel like emotionally it's hard

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:29.940
in a city like that is packed
and you're not used to it,

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:31.509
it's such a healing thing to have.

00:05:31.509 --> 00:05:33.890
- You need a reset every now and then

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:37.350
and just lower your vibration
and animals do that.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:38.183
They're pretty amazing.

00:05:38.183 --> 00:05:39.016
- [Kelly] You lower my vibration.

00:05:39.016 --> 00:05:40.160
You're very cool.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:42.000
You are so cool.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.322
We are obsessed with everything

00:05:43.322 --> 00:05:45.301
the Kindred Spirits Care Farm does,

00:05:45.301 --> 00:05:47.924
so we are giving the
sanctuary $5,000 to help out.

00:05:47.924 --> 00:05:48.983
(audience cheering)
- Oh my God.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:51.338
- Just buy all the Carrots.
- Thank you.

00:05:51.338 --> 00:05:53.988
All the carrots.
- All the carrots for Pierre.

